description: Seven standing UI-resilience rules — writes must be single-flight (no double submit / double charge), a component crash must stay contained to that component, the completion message must match the work that actually happened, no flow may be derived from state that has not loaded, local optimistic state must be rolled back like the cache is, a failed follow-up step must never route the user backwards, and a repeatable confirmation must replace itself instead of stacking. Applies to every mutating control, every composed surface, every success toast, every screen whose shape comes from a query, every optimistic edit held outside the cache, every multi-step flow that ends in a redirect, and every repeat-fire control.
